      "description": "Watch Central Cordoba vs Atletico Tucuman highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 31, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina action on July 31, 2026, brought together Central Córdoba and Atlético Tucumán in a clash of high stakes and tactical discipline. Fans expected a tightly contested affair, and the match delivered a narrative shaped by individual brilliance and defensive resilience. A Cagey Opening Period The first half was a story of two sides nullifying each other’s strengths. Central Córdoba looked to utilize their home advantage, pushing forward with intent, but Atlético Tucumán remained organized and disciplined at the back. Clear-cut chances were at a premium as the midfield battle dominated the proceedings. Both teams headed into the tunnel at halftime knowing that the second half would require a moment of magic to break the deadlock. Leandro Diaz Takes Charge As play resumed, the intensity shifted. A yellow card for Franco Nicola in the 52nd minute signaled a more aggressive approach from the visitors. That aggression paid off in the 63rd minute when Ramiro Ruiz delivered a pinpoint assist to Leandro Diaz , who clinicaly finished to give Atlético Tucumán the lead. The goal changed the complexion of the match , forcing Central Córdoba to throw more players forward in search of an equalizer. Late Drama and the Decisive Strike The closing stages were frantic as Central Córdoba made several tactical changes to salvage a point. However, their discipline wavered, resulting in a yellow card for Fernando Martinez in the 89th minute. Just as the home side pushed for a late miracle, Atlético Tucumán struck on the counter. In the 90+2 minute, Luis Ingolotti set up Leandro Diaz for his second goal of the night, effectively ending any hopes of a comeback. The referee blew the final whistle at 90+6 minutes, confirming a statement win for the visitors."
