      "description": "Watch Union Santa Fe vs Central Cordoba highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 11, 2026. The stands were packed on August 11, 2026, as Union Santa Fe hosted Central Cordoba in a highly anticipated Liga Profesional Argentina clash. Both sides sought to establish dominance early in a match that promised plenty of tactical intrigue. Union Takes the Initiative Union Santa Fe started the contest with intent, utilizing the home-field advantage to pin the visitors back. Their persistence paid off in the 17th minute when Julian Palacios delivered a precise pass to Lucas Menossi . The midfielder made no mistake, firing the ball home to give Union a deserved 1-0 lead. For the remainder of the first half, the hosts looked comfortable, controlling the tempo and limiting Central Cordoba to half-chances as they headed into the break with the advantage. A Stunning Second-Half Turnaround The dynamic of the match shifted dramatically shortly after the restart. Central Cordoba emerged for the second half with renewed energy and leveled the score in the 51st minute through a clinical finish from Michael Santos . Before the home side could even process the equalizer, they were dealt a second blow just three minutes later. In the 54th minute, Leonardo Sequeira turned provider, setting up Facundo Mansilla Zahir who found the back of the net to complete a rapid turnaround. Within a matter of minutes, Central Cordoba had transformed a deficit into a 1-2 lead, leaving the home supporters in stunned silence. Discipline Tested in the Closing Stages As the clock ticked down, the match became increasingly physical and frayed. A series of yellow cards illustrated the rising tension, with Lautaro Vargas , Leonardo Sequeira , and Horacio Tijanovich all entering the referee's book. Union Santa Fe attempted to find an equalizer by introducing fresh legs like Mauro Luna Diale , but the visitors' defense remained resolute. The drama continued deep into stoppage time as Yuri Casermeiro and Santiago Moyano also received cautions while trying to protect their lead. Despite seven minutes of added time and intense pressure from the hosts, Central Cordoba held firm to secure a hard-fought away victory, leaving Union Santa Fe to regret their second-half collapse."
